IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pea-types`
IMPORT `pea-eviction`
IMPORT `pea-notice-to-quit`
IMPORT `pea-penalty`

-- Protection from Eviction Act 1977 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "Must the owner go to court to recover possession from this occupier; is
--    the notice to quit valid and from when can it take effect; and, for the
--    landlord's conduct, is an offence made out, may a financial penalty be
--    imposed, up to how much, and by when must each step be taken?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Eviction case` HAS
    `the occupancy`                                     IS AN `Occupancy`
    `the notice to quit`                                IS A MAYBE `Notice to quit`
    `the conduct`                                       IS A MAYBE `Conduct`
    `the penalty facts`                                 IS A MAYBE `Penalty facts`

DECLARE `Eviction position` HAS
    `court proceedings required`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `excluded tenancy or licence`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice to quit meets s 5`                          IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `earliest day the notice can take effect`           IS A MAYBE DATE
    `offence under s 1`                                 IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `financial penalty may be imposed`                  IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `maximum financial penalty`                         IS A NUMBER
    `penalty dates`                                     IS A MAYBE `Penalty dates`

@ref ss 1, 1A, 2, 3, 3A, 5, 8, Sch A1
@export default The position under the Protection from Eviction Act 1977 (UK) for one occupier: whether the owner must use court proceedings to recover possession (ss 2, 3) and whether the letting is excluded (s 3A); if a notice to quit was given, whether it meets s 5 and the earliest day it can take effect; if the landlord's conduct is in question, whether it is an offence under s 1, whether a local housing authority may impose a financial penalty (s 1A), the maximum (£40,000), and the Schedule A1 dates. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS AN `Eviction case`  @desc The occupancy, any notice to quit, any conduct by the landlord, and the facts of any financial penalty
GIVETH AN `Eviction position`
`the eviction position for` c MEANS
    `Eviction position` WITH
        `court proceedings required`                    IS `court proceedings are required to recover possession from` o
        `excluded tenancy or licence`                   IS `is excluded` o
        `notice to quit meets s 5`                      IS
            CONSIDER c's `the notice to quit`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (`the notice meets s 5 for` o `and` n)
        `earliest day the notice can take effect`       IS
            CONSIDER c's `the notice to quit`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST n  THEN
                IF   `s 5 applies to` o `and` n
                THEN JUST (`the earliest day the notice can take effect for` o `and` n)
                ELSE NOTHING
        `offence under s 1`                             IS
            CONSIDER c's `the conduct`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN JUST (`an offence under s 1 is made out by` k)
        `financial penalty may be imposed`              IS
            CONSIDER c's `the conduct`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN
                CONSIDER c's `the penalty facts`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST p  THEN JUST (`a financial penalty may be imposed for` k `with` p)
        `maximum financial penalty`                     IS `the maximum financial penalty`
        `penalty dates`                                 IS
            CONSIDER c's `the penalty facts`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST p  THEN JUST (`the penalty dates for` p)
    WHERE
        o MEANS c's `the occupancy`
